WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.550
With a direct call, the caller names the operation
it wants another component to perform.

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:10.976
With implicit invocation, a component announces an
event and registered handlers react.

00:00:10.976 --> 00:00:16.838
A debugger can announce that execution stopped,
letting an editor highlight source without the

00:00:16.838 --> 00:00:20.018
debugger depending on that editor’s implementation.

00:00:20.018 --> 00:00:26.130
The same idea supports user-interface observers and
database triggers inside a single application.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:29.505
A laboratory announces that an experiment has
finished.

00:00:29.505 --> 00:00:35.336
The reporting service needs the result for a
summary, and an audit service needs it for its own

00:00:35.336 --> 00:00:35.765
record.

00:00:35.765 --> 00:00:41.657
If both merely compete to remove one message from
the same work queue, only one may receive each

00:00:41.657 --> 00:00:42.025
event.

00:00:42.025 --> 00:00:48.040
Independent reactions require separate subscription
progress or an equivalent fan-out arrangement.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:54.206
Within the reporting subscription, multiple workers
can share processing responsibility without

00:00:54.206 --> 00:00:56.673
changing the audit service's progress.

00:00:56.673 --> 00:01:02.709
The message still needs an explicit contract:
experiment identifier, event identifier, schema

00:01:02.709 --> 00:01:06.798
version and enough context to retrieve or interpret
the result.

00:01:06.798 --> 00:01:13.289
A broker can route messages, but cannot decide
whether the reporting service needs a snapshot of
the

00:01:13.289 --> 00:01:15.885
old result or may read its latest state.

00:01:15.885 --> 00:01:19.465
Draw the two subscriptions separately and fail one
consumer.

00:01:19.465 --> 00:01:23.044
Explain which backlog grows and whether the other
continues.

00:01:23.044 --> 00:01:28.771
This exercise connects asynchronous queue mechanisms
to event-driven structure while keeping the

00:01:28.771 --> 00:01:34.200
distinction between an instruction to one worker and
a fact announced to several consumers.
